Rank head-to-head on whether the reported problem is actually solved and every explicit requirement is met — not on code style, refactor cleanliness, verbosity, or effort shown. Do not reward or penalize language choice unless the instruction timeline requires a specific language.

Use only the evidence shown. Return STRICT JSON only, no prose:
{"rankings":[{"name":"<exact agent name>","breakdown":{"task":0,"grounding":0,"verification":0,"actionability":0},"evidence_level":"direct|mixed|narrative_only","dimension_reasons":{"task":"one concise sentence","grounding":"one concise sentence","verification":"one concise sentence","actionability":"one concise sentence"},"dimension_issue_ids":{"task":"none|unique_snake_case_issue","grounding":"none|unique_snake_case_issue","verification":"none|unique_snake_case_issue","actionability":"none|unique_snake_case_issue"},"caps":[],"strength":"one concise sentence","deduction":"one concise sentence or None","improve_dimension":"task|grounding|verification|actionability|none","improve":"one concrete improvement sentence or None"}],"winner":"<exact name>","winner_reason":"why this top-scoring candidate wins","tie_break":"substantive reason for an apparent tie, otherwise not_needed","summary":"concise overall comparison without generalizing a candidate-specific weakness"}

Include EVERY agent in rankings, best first, name copied EXACTLY. Every breakdown must use integers in the stated ranges. Do not include score; wtcp computes it from the breakdown, evidence_level, and declared hard caps. Every below-maximum dimension must have its own absolute-rubric justification in dimension_reasons and a unique lowercase snake_case dimension_issue_id; a maximum dimension should use issue ID none. Reusing an issue ID across genuinely deducted dimensions is forbidden because it double-charges one weakness. For Task specifically, the issue ID must name an actual missing/incorrect requirement or core answer defect. An issue ID containing unverified, unsupported, evidence, grounding, verification, citation, narrative, comparative, less_detailed, or fewer_details is invalid for Task, as is an omission-relative ID such as missed_x, overlooked_x, not_identified_x, or failed_to_identify_x unless it names an item the instruction timeline requested: put that concern in Grounding/Verification and keep Task at 4 unless it causes a concrete wrong answer or missing requested part. wtcp clears IDs for dimensions that normalize to full credit and namespaces shared hard-cap IDs by dimension. If the computed score is below 10, deduction must not be "None", improve_dimension must name ONE dimension that is actually below its maximum after evidence limits/caps, and improve must explain how to recover that dimension; never target a full-credit dimension. For a computed 10 use deduction/improve "None" and improve_dimension none. The winner must have a top absolute score; do not lower another candidate merely to avoid a tie. Give a substantive tie_break for an apparent tie, otherwise use not_needed; if wtcp creates a tie while applying evidence limits/caps, it replaces not_needed with an explicit judge-preference note. winner_reason must explain the selection consistently with the scores. summary should differ from winner_reason and compare the field without attributing one candidate's weakness to all candidates; an exact duplicate is omitted from the report. Follow the Output language rule exactly; keep JSON keys in English and every explanation concise.
EOF
}

_judge_one(){   # $1=path $2=task prompt $3=timeline $4=score round $5=pane_id $6=base ref -> "score|reason|model"
  local path="$1" prompt="$2" timeline="$3" score_round="$4" pane="$5" base="${6:-}" diff out req raw resp model score reason instr lang_rule rubric_line caps_line evidence_line dimension_lines adjustments_line
  local diff_chars combined_budget out_budget max_tokens repair_req repaired_model first_resp normalized
  local rubric_errf rubric_err="" first_err=""
  rubric_errf=$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/wtcp-rubric.XXXXXX") || rubric_errf="${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/wtcp-rubric.$$"
  local jhdr=(); [ -n "${COCKPIT_JUDGE_AUTH:-}" ] && jhdr+=(-H "Authorization: $COCKPIT_JUDGE_AUTH")
  [ -n "$path" ] && diff=$(_wt_diff "$path" "$base") || diff=""
  [ -n "$timeline" ] || timeline="[initial] ${prompt:-(unknown task)}"
  # Diff and terminal are one evidence pool. Analysis rounds with no changes
  # return the unused diff allocation to the terminal instead of wasting half
  # the context while truncating the actual deliverable.
  diff_chars=$(printf '%s' "$diff" | wc -c | tr -d ' ')
  combined_budget=$((COCKPIT_JUDGE_DIFF_CHARS+COCKPIT_JUDGE_OUTPUT_CHARS))
  out_budget=$(_judge_output_budget "$combined_budget" "$diff_chars" 800)
  out=$(_terminal_evidence "$pane" "$out_budget")
  instr=$(_judge_single_instructions)
  lang_rule=$(_judge_output_language_rule)
  max_tokens=$(_judge_single_max_tokens)
  req=$(jq -nc --arg s "$instr" --arg t "$timeline" --arg r "${score_round:-1}" --arg lang_rule "$lang_rule" --arg d "${diff:-(none)}" --arg o "$out" --arg m "${COCKPIT_JUDGE_MODEL:-}" \
    --argjson max_tokens "$max_tokens" \
    '{messages:[{role:"user",content:($s + "\n\nScore round: " + $r + "\nOutput language rule:\n" + $lang_rule + "\n\nInstruction timeline:\n" + $t + "\n\nDiff vs base (may be empty):\n" + $d + "\n\nAgent terminal output:\n" + $o)}],max_tokens:$max_tokens,temperature:0.2} + (if $m == "" then {} else {model:$m} end)')
  raw=$(curl -s --max-time "$COCKPIT_JUDGE_TIMEOUT" "$COCKPIT_JUDGE_URL" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' ${jhdr[@]+"${jhdr[@]}"} -d "$req" 2>/dev/null || true)
  model=$(printf '%s' "$raw" | jq -r '.model // empty' 2>/dev/null || true)
  resp=$(printf '%s' "$raw" | jq -r '.choices[0].message.content // empty' 2>/dev/null || true)
  if normalized=$(printf '%s' "$resp" | _rubric_response_normalize 0 2>"$rubric_errf"); then
    resp="$normalized"
  else
    first_resp="$resp"
    first_err=$(_rubric_error_summary < "$rubric_errf")

    first_err=$(_judge_rejection_detail "$resp" "$first_err")
    repair_req=$(printf '%s' "$req" | _judge_repair_request "$resp" "$max_tokens" "$first_err")
    raw=$(curl -s --max-time "$COCKPIT_JUDGE_TIMEOUT" "$COCKPIT_JUDGE_URL" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' ${jhdr[@]+"${jhdr[@]}"} -d "$repair_req" 2>/dev/null || true)
    repaired_model=$(printf '%s' "$raw" | jq -r '.model // empty' 2>/dev/null || true)
    [ -z "$repaired_model" ] || model="$repaired_model"
    resp=$(printf '%s' "$raw" | jq -r '.choices[0].message.content // empty' 2>/dev/null || true)
  fi
  if normalized=$(printf '%s' "$resp" | _rubric_response_normalize 0 2>"$rubric_errf"); then
    resp="$normalized"
    rm -f "$rubric_errf"
    score=$(printf '%s' "$resp" | jq -r '.score' 2>/dev/null)
    reason=$(printf '%s' "$resp" | jq -r '
      "- Strength: \(.strength)\n"
      + "- Deduction: \(.deduction)\n"
      + (if .improve_dimension == "none"
         then "- Improve: \(.improve)"
         else "- Improve [\(.improve_dimension)]: \(.improve)"
         end)
    ' 2>/dev/null)
    rubric_line=$(printf '%s' "$resp" | jq -r '"Rubric: Task \(.breakdown.task)/4 · Grounding \(.breakdown.grounding)/3 · Verification \(.breakdown.verification)/2 · Actionability \(.breakdown.actionability)/1"' 2>/dev/null)
    evidence_line=$(printf '%s' "$resp" | jq -r '"Evidence: \(.evidence_level)"' 2>/dev/null)
    dimension_lines=$(printf '%s' "$resp" | jq -r '"Dimension reasons:\n  Task [\(.dimension_issue_ids.task)]: \(.dimension_reasons.task)\n  Grounding [\(.dimension_issue_ids.grounding)]: \(.dimension_reasons.grounding)\n  Verification [\(.dimension_issue_ids.verification)]: \(.dimension_reasons.verification)\n  Actionability [\(.dimension_issue_ids.actionability)]: \(.dimension_reasons.actionability)"' 2>/dev/null)
    caps_line=$(printf '%s' "$resp" | jq -r '"Caps: " + (if (.caps | length) == 0 then "none" else (.caps | join(", ")) end)' 2>/dev/null)
    adjustments_line=$(printf '%s' "$resp" | jq -r '"Adjustments: " + (if ((.normalization_notes // []) | length) == 0 then "none" else (.normalization_notes | join("; ")) end)' 2>/dev/null)
    reason="${rubric_line}"$'\n'"${evidence_line}"$'\n'"${dimension_lines}"$'\n'"${caps_line}"$'\n'"${adjustments_line}"$'\n'"${reason}"
  else
    score=""
    rubric_err=$(_rubric_error_summary < "$rubric_errf"); rm -f "$rubric_errf"
    _record_invalid_judgment "independent candidate: ${path:-unknown}" "${model:-unknown}" \
      "FIRST RESPONSE REJECTED BECAUSE: ${first_err:-(unknown)}
${first_resp:-(empty response content)}

REPAIR RESPONSE REJECTED BECAUSE: ${rubric_err:-(unknown)}
${resp:-(empty response content)}"
    reason="invalid judgment after one JSON repair attempt — see $(_judge_invalid_file)"
  fi
  printf '%s|%s|%s' "${score:-?}" "${reason:-(no judgment — is the judge LLM running?)}" "${model:-(unknown)}"
}

_judge_file(){ printf '%s' "$HOME/.config/wtcp/judge.txt"; }
_diff_file(){ printf '%s' "$HOME/.config/wtcp/diff.txt"; }
_tmux_popup(){   # display-popup wrapper: optionally dim panes behind the modal
  local cwin="" old_style="" old_active_style="" rc restore=0 errexit=0
  cwin=$(_cur_win 2>/dev/null || true)
  if [ "${COCKPIT_POPUP_DIM:-1}" != 0 ] && [ -n "$cwin" ]; then
    old_style=$(tmux show-options -wqv -t "$cwin" window-style 2>/dev/null || printf 'default')
    old_active_style=$(tmux show-options -wqv -t "$cwin" window-active-style 2>/dev/null || printf 'default')
    tmux set-option -w -t "$cwin" window-style "$COCKPIT_POPUP_DIM_STYLE" 2>/dev/null || true
    tmux set-option -w -t "$cwin" window-active-style "$COCKPIT_POPUP_DIM_STYLE" 2>/dev/null || true
    restore=1
  fi
  case $- in *e*) errexit=1; set +e;; esac
  tmux display-popup "$@"
  rc=$?
  if [ "$restore" = 1 ]; then
    tmux set-option -w -t "$cwin" window-style "$old_style" 2>/dev/null
    tmux set-option -w -t "$cwin" window-active-style "$old_active_style" 2>/dev/null
  fi
  [ "$errexit" = 1 ] && set -e
  return "$rc"
}
# Full-diff popup for one agent worktree: the judge only sees a capped diff,
# the user gets the WHOLE thing. Renders through delta when on PATH (it
# colorizes plain diff itself), else colorized git diff + less.
_show_diff_popup(){   # $1=worktree name
  local wt="$1" path base F qF body pager color
  path=$(_wt_path "$wt")
  if [ -z "$path" ]; then
    tmux display-message "wtcp: no worktree path for [$wt]" 2>/dev/null || true
    echo "wtcp: no worktree path for [$wt]" >&2; return 1
  fi
  base=$(tmux show-options -wqv -t "$(_cur_win)" @cockpit_base 2>/dev/null || true)
  if command -v delta >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    # Force delta's pager to plain `less -R`: its default includes -F, which
    # would flash the popup shut on a one-screen diff (same gotcha as
    # _show_judge_report). delta wants an UNcolored diff on stdin.
    color=never; pager="DELTA_PAGER='less -R' delta <"
  else
    color=always; pager="LESS='-R' ${PAGER:-less}"
  fi
  body=$(_wt_diff_raw "$path" "$base" "$color")
  if [ -z "$body" ]; then
    tmux display-message "wtcp: [$wt] has no changes vs ${base:-main}" 2>/dev/null || true
    say "[$wt] has no changes vs ${base:-main}"
    return 0
  fi
  F=$(_diff_file); mkdir -p "$(dirname "$F")"
  printf '=== %s — diff vs %s ===\n\n%s\n' "$wt" "$(_diff_base "$path" "$base")" "$body" > "$F"
  qF=$(_sh_quote "$F")
  # NOTE: no -F on the pager (see _show_judge_report).
  _tmux_popup -E -w "$COCKPIT_POPUP_WIDTH" -h "$COCKPIT_POPUP_HEIGHT" "$pager $qF" 2>/dev/null || true
}
_show_judge_report(){
  local F="${1:-$(_judge_file)}" qF
  [ -s "$F" ] || { tmux display-message "wtcp: no judge report yet" 2>/dev/null || true; return 1; }
  qF=$(_sh_quote "$F")
  # NOTE: no -F — with -F less quits immediately when the report fits one screen,
  # which would make the popup flash and close. Keep it open until the user hits q.
  _tmux_popup -E -w "$COCKPIT_POPUP_WIDTH" -h "$COCKPIT_POPUP_HEIGHT" "LESS='-R' ${PAGER:-less} $qF" 2>/dev/null || true
}
# Collect "score<TAB>worktree" rows from the grid's scored pane borders, best
# score first. Unjudged panes (★ ?) get sort key -1 so they land LAST — '?' is
# text and would otherwise sort ABOVE the numbers under `sort -rn`. Name
# tie-break keeps the order deterministic among equal scores / multiple '?'.
_scored_rows(){   # $1=grid window id
  local cwin="$1" p wt label sc key rows=()
  while IFS= read -r p; do
    wt=$(pane_wt "$p"); [ -n "$wt" ] || continue
    label=$(tmux show-options -pqv -t "$p" @pane_label 2>/dev/null || true)
    case "$label" in *"★ "*) sc="${label##*★ }"; sc="${sc%% *}";; *) sc="";; esac
    case "$sc" in ''|*[!0-9.]*) sc="?";; esac
    key="$sc"; [ "$sc" = "?" ] && key="-1"
    rows+=("$key"$'\t'"$sc"$'\t'"$wt")
  done < <(tmux list-panes -t "$cwin" -F '#{pane_id}')
  [ "${#rows[@]}" -gt 0 ] || return 0
  printf '%s\n' "${rows[@]}" | sort -t"$(printf '\t')" -k1,1rn -k3,3 | cut -f2-
}
# Interactive menu over the grid's agents (best score first); selecting one runs
# `wtcp <verb> <worktree>`. No-ops when no client is attached (headless tests)
# or the grid has no agent panes.
_agent_menu(){   # $1=grid window $2=menu title $3=verb (pick|diff)
  local cwin="$1" title="$2" verb="$3" sess
  sess=$(tmux display -p -t "$cwin" '#{session_id}' 2>/dev/null || true)
  [ -n "$sess" ] && tmux list-clients -t "$sess" 2>/dev/null | grep -q . || return 0
  local items=() s n idx=0 key qn lbl
  while IFS=$'\t' read -r s n; do
    idx=$((idx+1)); key="$idx"; [ "$idx" -gt 9 ] && key=""
    qn=$(_sh_quote "$n")
    lbl="★ ${s}  ${n}"; [ "$s" = "?" ] && lbl="★ ?  ${n}  (unjudged)"
    items+=("$lbl" "$key" "run-shell \"$INVOKE_CMD $verb $qn\"")
  done < <(_scored_rows "$cwin")
  [ "${#items[@]}" -gt 0 ] || return 0
  items+=("" "" "" "Cancel" q "")
  tmux display-menu -T "$title" "${items[@]}" 2>/dev/null || true
}
_winner_menu(){ _agent_menu "$1" "wtcp — pick winner to merge" pick; }
_diff_menu(){   _agent_menu "$1" "wtcp — view agent diff" diff; }
_keep_menu(){   _agent_menu "$1" "wtcp — keep agent session (no merge)" keep; }
# The judge's winner, read from the scored pane borders: the 🏆-marked pane
# (comparative scoring), else the highest numeric ★ score (independent-scoring
# fallback stamps no trophy). Empty when nothing has been scored.
_scored_winner(){   # $1=grid window -> worktree name or ""
  local cwin="$1" p wt label
  while IFS= read -r p; do
    wt=$(pane_wt "$p"); [ -n "$wt" ] || continue
    label=$(tmux show-options -pqv -t "$p" @pane_label 2>/dev/null || true)
    case "$label" in *🏆*) printf '%s' "$wt"; return 0;; esac
  done < <(tmux list-panes -t "$cwin" -F '#{pane_id}')
  local s n
  while IFS=$'\t' read -r s n; do
    [ "$s" = "?" ] && continue
    printf '%s' "$n"; return 0
  done < <(_scored_rows "$cwin")
  return 0
}

# Fallback: judge each agent independently (used if comparative parsing fails).
_score_independent(){
  local cwin="$1" prompt="$2" timeline="$3" score_round="$4" base="$5"; shift 5
  local p wt path res rest sc reason reason_block model="" summary=""
  [ -n "$timeline" ] || timeline="[initial] ${prompt:-(unknown task)}"
  for p in "$@"; do
    wt=$(pane_wt "$p"); [ -n "$wt" ] || continue
    path=$(_wt_path "$wt")
    res=$(_judge_one "$path" "$prompt" "$timeline" "$score_round" "$p" "$base")   # "score|reason|model"; model is the last field
    sc="${res%%|*}"; rest="${res#*|}"; model="${rest##*|}"; reason="${rest%|*}"
    tmux set-option -p -t "$p" @pane_label "$wt   ★ $sc"
    tmux set-option -p -t "$p" @judge_reason "$reason"
    reason_block=$(printf '%s' "$reason" | sed 's/^/  /')
    summary="${summary}- ${wt}: ${sc}/10\n${reason_block}\n"
  done
  local F; F=$(_judge_file); mkdir -p "$(dirname "$F")"
  {
    printf 'Score round: %s\n' "${score_round:-1}"
    printf 'Instruction timeline:\n%s\n' "$timeline"
    printf 'Judge model: %s\n' "${model:-(unknown)}"
    printf 'Mode: independent fallback (comparative JSON remained invalid after one repair; diagnostic: %s)\n' "$(_judge_invalid_file)"
    printf 'Rubric: Task 0-4 · Grounding 0-3 · Verification 0-2 · Actionability 0-1\n\n'
    printf 'Rankings:\n%b' "$summary"
  } > "$F" 2>/dev/null || true
  _show_judge_report "$F"
}

# Comparative scoring: send ALL agents to the judge in one call so it ranks them
# head-to-head and picks a winner. Score (+winner) on each pane border + a
# popup with the comparison. Falls back to independent scoring if it can't parse.
cmd_score(){
  local fresh=0
  if [ "${1:-}" = "--fresh" ]; then fresh=1; shift; fi
  [ "$#" -eq 0 ] || die "score accepts only --fresh"
  need_tmux; goto_root
  if [ -z "${COCKPIT_JUDGE_URL:-}" ]; then
    tmux display-message "wtcp: set COCKPIT_JUDGE_URL in ~/.config/wtcp/config to use scoring" 2>/dev/null || true
    die "set COCKPIT_JUDGE_URL in ~/.config/wtcp/config to use scoring"
  fi
  _rotate_invalid_judgments
  local cwin prompt prompt_log score_round base; cwin=$(_cur_win)
  prompt=$(tmux show-options -wqv -t "$cwin" @cockpit_prompt 2>/dev/null || true)
  prompt_log=$(_prompt_log_get "$cwin")
  [ -n "$prompt_log" ] || prompt_log="[initial] ${prompt:-(unknown task)}"
  score_round=$(tmux show-options -wqv -t "$cwin" @cockpit_score_round 2>/dev/null || true)
  case "$score_round" in ''|*[!0-9]*) score_round=0 ;; esac
  score_round=$((score_round+1))
  tmux set-option -w -t "$cwin" @cockpit_score_round "$score_round" 2>/dev/null || true
  base=$(tmux show-options -wqv -t "$cwin" @cockpit_base 2>/dev/null || true)
  _style_window "$cwin"
  # Collect agent panes (skip the bar/empty panes).
  local p wt names=() panes=() prev_labels=() prev_reasons=() nag=0
  while IFS= read -r p; do
    wt=$(pane_wt "$p")
    if [ -z "$wt" ]; then tmux set-option -p -t "$p" @pane_label "$BAR_KEYS"; continue; fi
    if [ "$fresh" -eq 1 ]; then
      prev_labels+=(""); prev_reasons+=("")
    else
      prev_labels+=("$(tmux show-options -pqv -t "$p" @pane_label 2>/dev/null || true)")
      prev_reasons+=("$(tmux show-options -pqv -t "$p" @judge_reason 2>/dev/null || true)")
    fi
    names+=("$wt"); panes+=("$p"); nag=$((nag+1))
    tmux set-option -p -t "$p" @pane_label "$wt   judging..."
  done < <(tmux list-panes -t "$cwin" -F '#{pane_id}')
  [ "$nag" -ge 1 ] || { tmux display-message "wtcp: no agents to score" 2>/dev/null; return 0; }

  # Give each agent one combined pool. Change evidence initially targets half;
  # any unused portion flows to terminal evidence, which is the primary
  # deliverable for analysis/review rounds.
  local combined_per=$(( COCKPIT_JUDGE_COMPARE_CHARS / nag )); [ "$combined_per" -ge 1600 ] || combined_per=1600
  local change_target=$((combined_per/2)); [ "$change_target" -ge 800 ] || change_target=800
  local i blocks="" path diff out prev_label prev_reason diff_chars out_budget
  for (( i=0; i<nag; i++ )); do
    path=$(_wt_path "${names[i]}")
    [ -n "$path" ] && diff=$(_wt_diff "$path" "$base" "$change_target") || diff=""
    diff_chars=$(printf '%s' "$diff" | wc -c | tr -d ' ')
    out_budget=$(_judge_output_budget "$combined_per" "$diff_chars" 800)
    out=$(_terminal_evidence "${panes[i]}" "$out_budget")
    prev_label="${prev_labels[i]}"
    prev_reason="${prev_reasons[i]}"
    blocks="${blocks}"$'\n\n'"=== AGENT: ${names[i]} ==="$'\n'"--- Previous judge note (context only; may be absent) ---"$'\n'"${prev_label:-none}"$'\n'"${prev_reason:-}"$'\n'"--- Diff vs base (may be empty) ---"$'\n'"${diff}"$'\n'"--- Terminal output ---"$'\n'"${out}"
  done

  local jhdr=(); [ -n "${COCKPIT_JUDGE_AUTH:-}" ] && jhdr+=(-H "Authorization: $COCKPIT_JUDGE_AUTH")
  local instr req resp lang_rule max_tokens repair_req first_resp repaired_model normalized
  instr=$(_judge_compare_instructions)
  lang_rule=$(_judge_output_language_rule)
  max_tokens=$(_judge_compare_max_tokens "$nag")
  req=$(jq -nc --arg s "$instr" --arg t "$prompt_log" --arg r "$score_round" --arg lang_rule "$lang_rule" --arg b "$blocks" --arg m "${COCKPIT_JUDGE_MODEL:-}" \
    --argjson max_tokens "$max_tokens" \
    '{messages:[{role:"user",content:($s + "\n\nScore round: " + $r + "\nOutput language rule:\n" + $lang_rule + "\n\nInstruction timeline:\n" + $t + "\n\nAGENTS (compare these):" + $b)}],max_tokens:$max_tokens,temperature:0.2} + (if $m == "" then {} else {model:$m} end)')
  local raw model
  raw=$(curl -s --max-time "$COCKPIT_JUDGE_TIMEOUT" "$COCKPIT_JUDGE_URL" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' ${jhdr[@]+"${jhdr[@]}"} -d "$req" 2>/dev/null || true)
  model=$(printf '%s' "$raw" | jq -r '.model // empty' 2>/dev/null || true)
  resp=$(printf '%s' "$raw" | jq -r '.choices[0].message.content // empty' 2>/dev/null || true)

  local winner expected_names rubric_errf rubric_err="" first_err=""
  rubric_errf=$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/wtcp-rubric.XXXXXX") || rubric_errf="${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/wtcp-rubric.$$"
  expected_names=$(printf '%s\n' "${names[@]}" | jq -Rsc 'split("\n") | map(select(length > 0))')
  if normalized=$(printf '%s' "$resp" | _rubric_response_normalize "$nag" "$expected_names" 2>"$rubric_errf"); then
    resp="$normalized"
  else
    first_resp="$resp"
    first_err=$(_rubric_error_summary < "$rubric_errf")

    first_err=$(_judge_rejection_detail "$resp" "$first_err")
    repair_req=$(printf '%s' "$req" | _judge_repair_request "$resp" "$max_tokens" "$first_err")
    raw=$(curl -s --max-time "$COCKPIT_JUDGE_TIMEOUT" "$COCKPIT_JUDGE_URL" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' ${jhdr[@]+"${jhdr[@]}"} -d "$repair_req" 2>/dev/null || true)
    repaired_model=$(printf '%s' "$raw" | jq -r '.model // empty' 2>/dev/null || true)
    [ -z "$repaired_model" ] || model="$repaired_model"
    resp=$(printf '%s' "$raw" | jq -r '.choices[0].message.content // empty' 2>/dev/null || true)
  fi
  if normalized=$(printf '%s' "$resp" | _rubric_response_normalize "$nag" "$expected_names" 2>"$rubric_errf"); then
    resp="$normalized"
    rm -f "$rubric_errf"
  else
    rubric_err=$(_rubric_error_summary < "$rubric_errf"); rm -f "$rubric_errf"
    _record_invalid_judgment "comparative round ${score_round}" "${model:-unknown}" \
      "FIRST RESPONSE REJECTED BECAUSE: ${first_err:-(unknown)}
${first_resp:-(empty response content)}

REPAIR RESPONSE REJECTED BECAUSE: ${rubric_err:-(unknown)}
${resp:-(empty response content)}"
    _score_independent "$cwin" "$prompt" "$prompt_log" "$score_round" "$base" "${panes[@]}"   # couldn't parse -> per-agent fallback (re-judges, reports its own model)
    [ "$COCKPIT_NO_INTERACTIVE_MENUS" = "1" ] || _winner_menu "$cwin"
    return 0
  fi
  winner=$(printf '%s' "$resp" | jq -r '.winner // empty' 2>/dev/null || true)

  # Write the comparative report (jq formats the whole file).
  local F; F=$(_judge_file); mkdir -p "$(dirname "$F")"
  printf '%s' "$resp" | jq -r --arg timeline "$prompt_log" --arg round "$score_round" --arg model "${model:-(unknown)}" '
    def indent: split("\n") | map("  " + .) | join("\n");
    def rubric: "  Rubric: Task \(.breakdown.task)/4 · Grounding \(.breakdown.grounding)/3 · Verification \(.breakdown.verification)/2 · Actionability \(.breakdown.actionability)/1";
    def evidence: "  Evidence: \(.evidence_level)";
    def dimensions:
      "  Dimension reasons:\n"
      + "    Task [\(.dimension_issue_ids.task)]: \(.dimension_reasons.task)\n"
      + "    Grounding [\(.dimension_issue_ids.grounding)]: \(.dimension_reasons.grounding)\n"
      + "    Verification [\(.dimension_issue_ids.verification)]: \(.dimension_reasons.verification)\n"
      + "    Actionability [\(.dimension_issue_ids.actionability)]: \(.dimension_reasons.actionability)";
    def caps: "  Caps: " + (if (.caps | length) == 0 then "none" else (.caps | join(", ")) end);
    def adjustments: "  Adjustments: " + (if ((.normalization_notes // []) | length) == 0 then "none" else (.normalization_notes | join("; ")) end);
    def assessment:
      "  - Strength: \(.strength)\n"
      + "  - Deduction: \(.deduction)\n"
      + (if .improve_dimension == "none"
         then "  - Improve: \(.improve)"
         else "  - Improve [\(.improve_dimension)]: \(.improve)"
         end);
    .winner as $w
    | "Score round: \($round)\n"
      + "Instruction timeline:\n\($timeline)\n"
      + "Judge model: \($model)\n\n"
      + "Rubric: Task 0-4 · Grounding 0-3 · Verification 0-2 · Actionability 0-1\n\n"
      + (if $w then "Winner: \($w)\n\n" else "" end)
      + "Winner rationale:\n\(.winner_reason)\n"
      + "Tie-break:\n\(.tie_break)\n\n"
      + (if ((.summary // "") != "" and .summary != .winner_reason)
         then "Summary:\n" + .summary + "\n\n"
         else ""
         end)
      + "Rankings:\n"
      + ([.rankings[] | "- \(.name): \(.score)/10\(if .name==$w then " (winner)" else "" end)\n" + rubric + "\n" + evidence + "\n" + dimensions + "\n" + caps + "\n" + adjustments + "\n" + assessment] | join("\n"))
  ' > "$F" 2>/dev/null || true

  # Stamp each pane border with its ★score (+🏆 winner).
  local nm sc rs mark
  while IFS=$'\t' read -r nm sc rs; do
    for (( i=0; i<nag; i++ )); do
      [ "${names[i]}" = "$nm" ] || continue
      mark=""; [ "$nm" = "$winner" ] && mark=" 🏆"
      tmux set-option -p -t "${panes[i]}" @pane_label "${names[i]}   ★ ${sc}${mark}"
      tmux set-option -p -t "${panes[i]}" @judge_reason "$rs"
    done
  done < <(printf '%s' "$resp" | jq -r '.rankings[] | [
    .name,
    (.score|tostring),
    ("Rubric: Task \(.breakdown.task)/4 · Grounding \(.breakdown.grounding)/3 · Verification \(.breakdown.verification)/2 · Actionability \(.breakdown.actionability)/1\n"
      + "Evidence: \(.evidence_level)\n"
      + "Dimension reasons:\n"
      + "  Task [\(.dimension_issue_ids.task)]: \(.dimension_reasons.task)\n"
      + "  Grounding [\(.dimension_issue_ids.grounding)]: \(.dimension_reasons.grounding)\n"
      + "  Verification [\(.dimension_issue_ids.verification)]: \(.dimension_reasons.verification)\n"
      + "  Actionability [\(.dimension_issue_ids.actionability)]: \(.dimension_reasons.actionability)\n"
      + "Caps: " + (if (.caps | length) == 0 then "none" else (.caps | join(", ")) end)
      + "\nAdjustments: " + (if ((.normalization_notes // []) | length) == 0 then "none" else (.normalization_notes | join("; ")) end)
      + "\n- Strength: \(.strength)"
      + "\n- Deduction: \(.deduction)"
      + (if .improve_dimension == "none"
         then "\n- Improve: \(.improve)"
         else "\n- Improve [\(.improve_dimension)]: \(.improve)"
         end))
  ] | @tsv' 2>/dev/null)
  # Any agent the judge skipped -> mark unknown so the border isn't stuck on "judging...".
  for (( i=0; i<nag; i++ )); do
    case "$(tmux show-options -pqv -t "${panes[i]}" @pane_label 2>/dev/null)" in
      *"★ "*) ;; *) tmux set-option -p -t "${panes[i]}" @pane_label "${names[i]}   ★ ?";;
    esac
  done

  _show_judge_report "$F" || true
  # Winner is now resolvable non-interactively: `wtcp merge` merges it one-shot.
  [ -n "$winner" ] && say "winner [$winner] — merge it with 'wtcp merge' (prefix Ctrl-R also offers it)"
  # After reading the report, offer a one-key winner pick that merges directly.
  [ "$COCKPIT_NO_INTERACTIVE_MENUS" = "1" ] || _winner_menu "$cwin"
}

# Show or set the agent set compared by `wtcp start` (persists to ~/.config/wtcp/config).
cmd_agents(){
  if [ "$#" -eq 0 ]; then
    echo "$COCKPIT_AGENTS"
    _warn_agent_problems_short "$COCKPIT_AGENTS" || return 1
    return 0
  fi
  [ "$#" -le 6 ] || die "at most 6 agents are supported (got $#)"
  mkdir -p "$(dirname "$WTCP_CONFIG")"
  local val="$*"
  _validate_agents "$val"
  if [ -f "$WTCP_CONFIG" ] && grep -q '^COCKPIT_AGENTS=' "$WTCP_CONFIG"; then
    awk -v v="COCKPIT_AGENTS=\"$val\"" '/^COCKPIT_AGENTS=/{print v;next}{print}' "$WTCP_CONFIG" > "$WTCP_CONFIG.tmp" && mv "$WTCP_CONFIG.tmp" "$WTCP_CONFIG"
  else
    printf 'COCKPIT_AGENTS="%s"\n' "$val" >> "$WTCP_CONFIG"
